From: Richard Osterloh <richard.osterloh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] zephyr: tcp: write the whole buffer, not what fits in the window

Zephyr's TCP send() queues only what fits in the send window and returns
that count. _z_tcp_zephyr_write returned it unchanged, and
_z_link_send_wbuf treats any short write on a stream link as
_Z_ERR_TRANSPORT_TX_FAILED -- after the prefix is already in the stream.
The peer then reads the following batches as the rest of the truncated one
and drops the session with a decoding error.

Seen on an ESP32 (NET_BUF_TX_COUNT=36, NET_BUF_DATA_SIZE=128) declaring a
ROS node through Pico-ROS: the burst of declarations fills the ~1.5 KB send
window at the same byte every session, rmw_zenohd logs "RX task failed ...
decoding error", and auto-reconnect replays the burst into the same wall.

Loop until the whole buffer is written, as _z_tcp_zephyr_read_exact already
does for reads. send() returning <= 0 is still reported as a failure.
---
diff --git a/src/link/transport/tcp/tcp_zephyr.c b/src/link/transport/tcp/tcp_zephyr.c
index bca917a5..859729b9 100644
--- a/src/link/transport/tcp/tcp_zephyr.c
+++ b/src/link/transport/tcp/tcp_zephyr.c
@@ -220,7 +220,18 @@ static size_t _z_tcp_zephyr_read_exact(_z_sys_net_socket_t sock, uint8_t *ptr, s
 }
 
 static size_t _z_tcp_zephyr_write(_z_sys_net_socket_t sock, const uint8_t *ptr, size_t len) {
-    return (size_t)send(sock._fd, ptr, len, 0);
+    // Zephyr's TCP send() queues only what fits in the send window and returns
+    // that count, and _z_link_send_wbuf treats a short write on a stream link as
+    // fatal after the prefix is already on the wire. Write it all, like the read.
+    size_t n = 0;
+    while (n < len) {
+        ssize_t wb = send(sock._fd, &ptr[n], len - n, 0);
+        if (wb <= 0) {
+            return SIZE_MAX;
+        }
+        n += (size_t)wb;
+    }
+    return n;
 }
 
 z_result_t _z_tcp_endpoint_init(_z_sys_net_endpoint_t *ep, const char *address, const char *port) {
